<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Hausdorff Measure and Hausdorff Dimension</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To make our theoretical discussions self-contained, we briefly review the definitions and basic properties of Hausdorff measure and Hausdorff dimension. These concepts provide finer notions of “size” than Lebesgue outer measure, especially for sets of measure zero. The definitions and the properties that are useful for our proofs listed below follow standard references in fractal geometry; for a comprehensive treatment, we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hausdorff Measure.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-negative number. For any <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{\delta}^{d}(F)=\inf\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\operatorname{diam}(U_{i})^{d}\,\middle|\,F\subseteq\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}U_{i},\operatorname{diam}(U_{i})\leq\delta\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mi>diam</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>diam</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\delta}^{d}(F)=\inf\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\operatorname{diam}(U_{i})^{d}\,\middle|\,F\subseteq\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}U_{i},\operatorname{diam}(U_{i})\leq\delta\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{diam}(U):=\sup\left\{|x-y|\mid x,y\in U\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diam</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{diam}(U):=\sup\left\{|x-y|\mid x,y\in U\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the diameter of <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional Hausdorff measure of <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d}(F):=\lim_{\delta\to 0}H_{\delta}^{d}(F)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d}(F):=\lim_{\delta\to 0}H_{\delta}^{d}(F).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hausdorff Dimension.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Hausdorff dimension of <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(F)=\inf\left\{d\geq 0\mid H^{d}(F)=0\right\}=\sup\left\{d\mid H^{d}(F)=\infty\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(F)=\inf\left\{d\geq 0\mid H^{d}(F)=0\right\}=\sup\left\{d\mid H^{d}(F)=\infty\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a subset of <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-negative number. The following properties hold:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Monotonicity) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subseteq F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subseteq F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d}(E)\leq H^{d}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d}(E)\leq H^{d}(F)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(E)\leq\dim_{H}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(E)\leq\dim_{H}(F)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Countable Subadditivity) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\bigcup_{i=1}^{\infty}F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\bigcup_{i=1}^{\infty}F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d}(F)\leq\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}H^{d}(F_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d}(F)\leq\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}H^{d}(F_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Countable Stability) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\bigcup_{i=1}^{\infty}F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\bigcup_{i=1}^{\infty}F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(F)=\sup_{1\leq i&lt;\infty}\{dim_{H}(F_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(F)=\sup_{1\leq i&lt;\infty}\{dim_{H}(F_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Countable sets) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is countable, then </span><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(F)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(F)=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, Hausdorff measure generalizes familiar notions such as length, area, and volume to arbitrary real dimensions. Hausdorff dimension of a set is the critical threshold at which this measure drops from infinity to zero, quantifying how “dense” or “complex” the set is at arbitrarily small scales.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>No-Free-Lunch Theorem of LG</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No-Free-Lunch Theorem of LG states that the average performance of any two learning algorithms over all possible target concepts is identical.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No-Free-Lunch Theorem of LG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For some <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider two sets <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}=\Sigma^{[N_{0}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}=\Sigma^{[N_{0}]}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}_{N}=\Sigma^{[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}_{N}=\Sigma^{[N]}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set.
Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}\in{\mathcal{F}}(:={\mathcal{F}}_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N},{\mathcal{Y}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mspace style="width:0.389em;" width="0.389em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}\in{\mathcal{F}}(:={\mathcal{F}}_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N},{\mathcal{Y}}})</annotation></semantics></math> be two concepts such that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(x)=c_{2}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(x)=c_{2}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c\mid{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\right):=\left\{f\in{\mathcal{F}}\mid f(x)=c(x)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c\mid{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\right):=\left\{f\in{\mathcal{F}}\mid f(x)=c(x)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}}^{\prime}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:{\mathcal{Y}}\times{\mathcal{Y}}\mapsto{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:{\mathcal{Y}}\times{\mathcal{Y}}\mapsto{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the loss function. For any distribution <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}\left({\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})\right)={\mathcal{X}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}\left({\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})\right)={\mathcal{X}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{f\in{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c_{1}|_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}}\right)}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})}\left[\ell\left(c_{1}(x),f(x)\right)\right]=\sum_{f\in{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c_{2}|_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}}\right)}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})}\left[\ell\left(c_{2}(x),f(x)\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{f\in{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c_{1}|_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}}\right)}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})}\left[\ell\left(c_{1}(x),f(x)\right)\right]=\sum_{f\in{\mathcal{F}}/\left(c_{2}|_{{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}}\right)}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim{\mathcal{D}}({\mathcal{X}}_{N})}\left[\ell\left(c_{2}(x),f(x)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="5No-Free-Lunch Theorem of LG []. ‣ Appendix B No-Free-Lunch Theorem of LG ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> implies that no learning algorithm can universally achieve length generalization across all possible target functions. Consequently, incorporating prior knowledge about the target becomes essential for selecting algorithms or designing models capable of LG.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We note that the negative results, i.e., the limitations of PEs, are independent of the above No-Free-Lunch Theorem. We show that when shifting from short to long instances requires “new operators”, LG cannot be achieved solely by adapting the PE, even under perfect prior knowledge.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Different Implementations of PEs</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PEs may share the same PRFs but differ in their concrete implementations.
In the following subsections, we present distinct implementations of the same PRF <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:{\mathbb{N}}\times{\mathbb{N}}\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:{\mathbb{N}}\times{\mathbb{N}}\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we consider sequences up to length <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and the PRF <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi([N]\times[N])\subseteq[S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi([N]\times[N])\subseteq[S]</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the input sequence by <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}^{(l)}=\left(h_{1}^{(l)},\dots,h_{n}^{(l)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{(l)}=\left(h_{1}^{(l)},\dots,h_{n}^{(l)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and the query-key weight by <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> for layer <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">C-A</span> </span><span id="A3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Learnable PE</span></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In learnable PE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, we encode the PRF with learnable embedding vectors. Two pairs <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are encoded with the same embedding vector if <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j)=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j)=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. The PE vectors are typically added to the hidden states. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in{\mathbb{R}}^{S\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in{\mathbb{R}}^{S\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the learnable embedding vectors. Then the query-key weight is computed as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}=\left(h_{j}^{(l-1)}+P_{\phi(i,j)}^{(l)}\right)^{\intercal}W_{K}^{(l)\intercal}W_{Q}^{(l)}h_{i}^{(l-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}=\left(h_{j}^{(l-1)}+P_{\phi(i,j)}^{(l)}\right)^{\intercal}W_{K}^{(l)\intercal}W_{Q}^{(l)}h_{i}^{(l-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above implementation adds the PE vectors to the hidden states only when computing the keys. We can also add the PE vectors when computing the queries and the values, though these may have little effect on the performance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">C-B</span> </span><span id="A3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rotary PE</span></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rotary PE (RoPE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite> uses multiplication instead of addition to incorporate positional information. For a sequence <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}=\left(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}=\left(x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, it seeks embedding functions <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{Q},f_{K}:{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times\mapsto[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">×</mo><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{Q},f_{K}:{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times\mapsto[N]</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle f_{Q}(x_{i},i),f_{K}(x_{j},j)\right\rangle=g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle f_{Q}(x_{i},i),f_{K}(x_{j},j)\right\rangle=g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some function <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times[S]\mapsto{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{d}\times[S]\mapsto{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If there exist two functions <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}:[N]\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}:[N]\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{2}:[N]\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{2}:[N]\mapsto{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j)=\phi_{1}(i)-\phi_{2}(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j)=\phi_{1}(i)-\phi_{2}(j)</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}f_{Q}(x_{i},i)=R^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}W_{Q}x_{i},\\
f_{K}(x_{j},j)=R^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}W_{K}x_{j},\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}f_{Q}(x_{i},i)=R^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}W_{Q}x_{i},\\
f_{K}(x_{j},j)=R^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}W_{K}x_{j},\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}R^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\\
R^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}R^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi_{1}(i)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\\
R^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi_{2}(j)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with the hyperparameter <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=\{\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{d/2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=\{\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{d/2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If the PRF <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be decomposed as the different of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{2}(j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{2}(j)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can compute <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> directly:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)=\left(W_{Q}x_{i}\right)^{\intercal}R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}\left(W_{K}x_{j}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\left(x_{i},x_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)=\left(W_{Q}x_{i}\right)^{\intercal}R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}\left(W_{K}x_{j}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos\phi(i,j)\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The query-key weight is computed as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}=g\left(h^{(l-1)}_{i},h^{(l-1)}_{j},\phi(i,j)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i,j}^{(l)}=g\left(h^{(l-1)}_{i},h^{(l-1)}_{j},\phi(i,j)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">While LBPE is implemented with learnable PE in Section <a href="#S6" title="VI Extensions ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI</span></a>, it can also be combined with RoPE. If we have prior knowledge or a belief that the target PRF is decomposable, we consider two models <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}_{1}(\cdot;w_{1}),\tilde{\phi_{2}}(\cdot;w_{2}):[N]\mapsto\Delta^{[S]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}_{1}(\cdot;w_{1}),\tilde{\phi_{2}}(\cdot;w_{2}):[N]\mapsto\Delta^{[S]}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},w_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},w_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are learnable parameters. We replace <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Theta,i}^{Q,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Theta,i}^{Q,d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\Theta,j}^{K,d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\Theta,j}^{K,d}</annotation></semantics></math> with their learning-based variants <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{\Theta,i}^{Q,d}(w_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{\Theta,i}^{Q,d}(w_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{\Theta,j}^{K,d}(w_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{\Theta,j}^{K,d}(w_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\tilde{R}^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}(w_{1})=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}_{1}(i;w_{1})\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\\
\tilde{R}^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}(w_{2})=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}_{2}(j;w_{2})\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\tilde{R}^{Q,d}_{\Theta,i}(w_{1})=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}_{1}(i;w_{1})\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},\\
\tilde{R}^{K,d}_{\Theta,j}(w_{2})=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}_{2}(j;w_{2})\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In the general case, we can replace <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> with its learning-based counterpart <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> defined as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}(w)=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}(i,j;w)\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋱</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}^{Q,K,d}_{\Theta,i,j}(w)=\sum_{s\in[S]}\left[\tilde{\phi}(i,j;w)\right]_{s}\begin{bmatrix}\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\sin s\theta_{1}&amp;\cos s\theta_{1}&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0\\
\vdots&amp;\vdots&amp;\ddots&amp;\vdots&amp;\vdots\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}&amp;-\sin s\theta_{d/2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;\sin s\theta_{d/2}&amp;\cos s\theta_{d/2}\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\cdot,\cdot;w):[N]\times[N]\mapsto\Delta^{[S]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\cdot,\cdot;w):[N]\times[N]\mapsto\Delta^{[S]}</annotation></semantics></math> is the LBPRF with the learnable parameter <math id="A3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">D-A</span> </span><span id="A4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="1. ‣ IV Warmup: A Study in POLAs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(B)&lt;\dim_{H}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(B)&lt;\dim_{H}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(A\setminus B)=\dim_{H}(A),\text{ and }H^{\dim_{H}(A)}(A\setminus B)=H^{\dim_{H}(A)}(A)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(A\setminus B)=\dim_{H}(A),\text{ and }H^{\dim_{H}(A)}(A\setminus B)=H^{\dim_{H}(A)}(A).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof for Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="1. ‣ D-A Proof for Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For notation simplicity, define <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}:=\dim_{H}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}:=\dim_{H}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(A\setminus B)&lt;d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(A\setminus B)&lt;d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists a <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left\{\dim_{H}(A\setminus B),\dim_{H}(B)\right\}&lt;d^{\prime}&lt;d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left\{\dim_{H}(A\setminus B),\dim_{H}(B)\right\}&lt;d^{\prime}&lt;d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the countable subadditivity of the Hausdorff measure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq H^{d^{\prime}}(A)\leq H^{d^{\prime}}(A\setminus B)+H^{d^{\prime}}(B)=0+0=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq H^{d^{\prime}}(A)\leq H^{d^{\prime}}(A\setminus B)+H^{d^{\prime}}(B)=0+0=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we obtain that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d^{\prime}}(A)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d^{\prime}}(A)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts the definition of the Hausdorff dimension <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to prove that <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)=H^{d_{A}}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)=H^{d_{A}}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}(B)&lt;\dim_{H}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}(B)&lt;\dim_{H}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{A}}(B)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{A}}(B)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. On the one hand, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{A}}(A)\leq H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)+H^{d_{A}}(B)=H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{A}}(A)\leq H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)+H^{d_{A}}(B)=H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{A}}(A)\geq H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{A}}(A)\geq H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)=H^{d_{A}}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{A}}(A\setminus B)=H^{d_{A}}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}:=\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\right)=\frac{N(N+1)}{2}-\frac{N_{0}(N_{0}+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}:=\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\right)=\frac{N(N+1)}{2}-\frac{N_{0}(N_{0}+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{0}}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\right)=(2M)^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{0}}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\right)=(2M)^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}S_{1}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid 1\leq i\leq j\leq N_{0}\right\},\\
S_{2}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid N_{0}&lt;i\leq j\leq N\right\}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}S_{1}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid 1\leq i\leq j\leq N_{0}\right\},\\
S_{2}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid N_{0}&lt;i\leq j\leq N\right\}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all functions from <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}\cup\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}\cup\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}:=\left\{I:S_{2}\mapsto S_{1}\cup\{0\}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}:=\left\{I:S_{2}\mapsto S_{1}\cup\{0\}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the subset of non-increasing LRC, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{A\in{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\mid\operatorname{LRC}(A;{\mathcal{X}},N_{0})=\operatorname{LRC}(A;{\mathcal{X}},N)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>LRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{A\in{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\mid\operatorname{LRC}(A;{\mathcal{X}},N_{0})=\operatorname{LRC}(A;{\mathcal{X}},N)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Then we have <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}=\bigcup_{I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}}\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}=\bigcup_{I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}}\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A4.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}:=\left\{A\in{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\,\middle|\,\text{for all }(i,j)\in S_{2},\ \begin{cases}A_{i,j}=A_{I(i,j)}&amp;\text{if }I(i,j)\neq 0,\\
A_{i,j}=0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mtext>for all </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}:=\left\{A\in{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\,\middle|\,\text{for all }(i,j)\in S_{2},\ \begin{cases}A_{i,j}=A_{I(i,j)}&amp;\text{if }I(i,j)\neq 0,\\
A_{i,j}=0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left(\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left(\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, by the countable stability of Hausdorff dimension <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left(\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=\max_{I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}}\left\{\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}\right\}=0&lt;d_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left(\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=\max_{I\in{\mathcal{I}}_{N_{0},N}}\left\{\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{I}\right\}=0&lt;d_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}={\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\setminus\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}={\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}\setminus\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="1. ‣ D-A Proof for Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=d_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=d_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed learning algorithm, the learned parameter is determined by the chosen PRF <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and the sub-matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}</annotation></semantics></math> of the target. Denote the parameter learned with the PRF <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and the sub-matrix <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{N_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}\in{\mathcal{U}}_{N_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\phi,B_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\phi,B_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, we define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}:=\left\{A_{\phi,B_{0}}\mid\phi\in\Phi_{N,S}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}:=\left\{A_{\phi,B_{0}}\mid\phi\in\Phi_{N,S}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi_{N,S}:=\left\{\phi\mid\phi:[N]\times[N]\mapsto[S]\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{N,S}:=\left\{\phi\mid\phi:[N]\times[N]\mapsto[S]\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{N,S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{N,S}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}\right)=0&lt;d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}\right)=0&lt;d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{A}}_{B_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)\leq\dim_{H}\left(A\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)\leq\dim_{H}\left(A\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=0&lt;d_{0}=\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left({\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=0&lt;d_{0}=\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="1. ‣ D-A Proof for Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=\dim_{H}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{N}=d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{N}=d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, it also holds that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{d_{N}}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=H^{d_{N}}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{d_{N}}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right)=H^{d_{N}}\left(\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{M,B_{0}}^{N_{0},N}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">D-B</span> </span><span id="A4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="2. ‣ IV Warmup: A Study in POLAs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As in the proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="1. ‣ IV Warmup: A Study in POLAs ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}S_{1}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid 1\leq i\leq j\leq N_{0}\right\},\\
S_{2}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid N_{0}&lt;i\leq j\leq N\right\}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}S_{1}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid 1\leq i\leq j\leq N_{0}\right\},\\
S_{2}^{N_{0},N}:=\left\{(i,j)\mid N_{0}&lt;i\leq j\leq N\right\}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}\right)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}\right)+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}\right)=\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>LRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N_{0}}\right)=\operatorname{LRC}\left(f^{*},{\mathcal{X}}_{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
there exist <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},\cdots,U_{S-1}\in\{0,1\}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},\cdots,U_{S-1}\in\{0,1\}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle U_{s},U_{s}^{\prime}\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle U_{s},U_{s}^{\prime}\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\mathds{1}_{N_{0}\times N_{0}}\right\rangle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\mathds{1}_{N_{0}\times N_{0}}\right\rangle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}=\sum_{s=1}^{S-1}a_{s}U_{s},a_{s}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}=\sum_{s=1}^{S-1}a_{s}U_{s},a_{s}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,\dots,S-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,\dots,S-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
then for each <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\in S_{2}^{N_{0},N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\in S_{2}^{N_{0},N}</annotation></semantics></math>, either <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{i,j}=A^{*}_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{i,j}=A^{*}_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})\in S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})\in S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{N_{0}\times N_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{N_{0}\times N_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}\times N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}\times N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix whose entries are all ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j)=\begin{cases}s,&amp;\text{if }\left(U_{s}\right)_{i,j}=1,\\
S,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j)=\begin{cases}s,&amp;\text{if }\left(U_{s}\right)_{i,j}=1,\\
S,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The PE induced by the PRF <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\phi}=\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}^{\phi}q_{s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\phi}=\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}^{\phi}q_{s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1},\dots,q_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1},\dots,q_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are learnable parameters and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(U_{s}^{\phi}\right)_{i,j}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }\phi(i,j)=s,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(U_{s}^{\phi}\right)_{i,j}=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }\phi(i,j)=s,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,\dots,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,\dots,S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We show the POLA model with the above PE initialized at 0 and trained with gradient descent achieves <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{0},N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{0},N)</annotation></semantics></math>-LG. Notice that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{\phi}\right)=\sum_{s=1}^{S}\left\langle xe_{n}^{\intercal},U_{s}\right\rangle q_{s}:=f(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>POLA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{\phi}\right)=\sum_{s=1}^{S}\left\langle xe_{n}^{\intercal},U_{s}\right\rangle q_{s}:=f(q)</annotation></semantics></math> is linear w.r.t. to the learnable parameters <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\left[q_{1},\dots,q_{S}\right]^{\intercal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\left[q_{1},\dots,q_{S}\right]^{\intercal}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the learned interpolator <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})</annotation></semantics></math> is that minimizes the <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}=\argmin\|q\|_{2},\text{ s.t. }f(x,n;q)=f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{*}\right)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> s.t. </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>POLA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}=\argmin\|q\|_{2},\text{ s.t. }f(x,n;q)=f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{*}\right)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is an interpolator for all <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}\hat{q}_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}=A^{*}_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}=\left(\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}a_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}\hat{q}_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}=A^{*}_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}=\left(\sum_{s=1}^{S}U_{s}a_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,\dots,S-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,\dots,S-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\left(\sum_{s^{\prime}=1}^{S}U_{s^{\prime}}\hat{q}_{s^{\prime}}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle=\left\langle\left(\sum_{s^{\prime}=1}^{S}U_{s^{\prime}}a_{s^{\prime}}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\left(\sum_{s^{\prime}=1}^{S}U_{s^{\prime}}\hat{q}_{s^{\prime}}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle=\left\langle\left(\sum_{s^{\prime}=1}^{S}U_{s^{\prime}}a_{s^{\prime}}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle\hat{q}_{s}=\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle a_{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle\hat{q}_{s}=\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle a_{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]},\left(U_{s}\right)_{[N_{0}],[N_{0}]}\right\rangle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{s}=a_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{s}=a_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,\dots,S-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,\dots,S-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{q\mid f(x,n;q)=f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{*}\right)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]\right\}\subseteq\{q\mid q_{s}=a_{s}\text{ for all }s=1,\dots,S-1\}:=Q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>POLA</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mtext> for all </mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mtext> for all </mtext><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{q\mid f(x,n;q)=f_{\text{POLA}}\left(x,n;A^{*}\right)\text{ for all }x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]\right\}\subseteq\{q\mid q_{s}=a_{s}\text{ for all }s=1,\dots,S-1\}:=Q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that when <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{S}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{S}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the function <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})</annotation></semantics></math> interpolates the training data, and <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}=\argmin_{q\in Q}\|q\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}=\argmin_{q\in Q}\|q\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the learned model is <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\cdot;\hat{q})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}=\left[a_{1},\dots,a_{S-1},0\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}=\left[a_{1},\dots,a_{S-1},0\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,n;\hat{q})=f_{\text{POLA}}(x,n;A^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>POLA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,n;\hat{q})=f_{\text{POLA}}(x,n;A^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{X}},n\in[N_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the model achieves <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{0},N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{0},N)</annotation></semantics></math>-LG.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A4.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">D-C</span> </span><span id="A4.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="3. ‣ V-B Limitations of PEs ‣ V PEs for LG in Practical Transformers ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}:=\left\{f_{0}\,\middle|\,f_{0}:\{0,1\}^{[N_{0}]}\mapsto\{0,1\}^{K}\right\},\Phi_{N,S}:=\left\{\phi:[N]\times[N]\mapsto[S]\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}:=\left\{f_{0}\,\middle|\,f_{0}:\{0,1\}^{[N_{0}]}\mapsto\{0,1\}^{K}\right\},\Phi_{N,S}:=\left\{\phi:[N]\times[N]\mapsto[S]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed learning algorithm, the learned model is determined by the target function restricted on <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1\}^{[N_{0}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1\}^{[N_{0}]}</annotation></semantics></math> and the PE. In other words, each pair <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(u,\phi\right)\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}\times\Phi_{N,S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(u,\phi\right)\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}\times\Phi_{N,S}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a model (denoted by <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{u,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{u,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>) learned by the algorithm. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all these models, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}:=\left\{f_{u,\phi}\mid u\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}},\phi\in\Phi_{N,S}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}:=\left\{f_{u,\phi}\mid u\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}},\phi\in\Phi_{N,S}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}|\leq\left|{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}\right|\leq|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}||\Phi_{N,S}|=2^{K\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}2^{n}}\times S^{N^{2}}=2^{K\left(2^{N_{0}+1}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}|\leq\left|{\mathcal{F}}^{\prime}_{N_{0},\Phi_{N,S}}\right|\leq|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}||\Phi_{N,S}|=2^{K\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}2^{n}}\times S^{N^{2}}=2^{K\left(2^{N_{0}+1}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be the subset of functions with non-increasing SRC, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}:=\left\{f\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\mid\operatorname{SRC}(f,N_{0})=\operatorname{SRC}(f,N)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>SRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>SRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}:=\left\{f\in{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\mid\operatorname{SRC}(f,N_{0})=\operatorname{SRC}(f,N)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}\right|\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}=2^{K\left(2^{N_{0}+1}-1\right)}\times\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0}}\right|\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}=2^{K\left(2^{N_{0}+1}-1\right)}\times\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since</p>
<table id="A4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}\geq\frac{\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|-\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|-\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|-\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}\geq\frac{\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|-\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|-\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|-\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|</annotation></semantics></math> are monotonously increasing w.r.t. <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to consider <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}=N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}=N-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq 2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}},\\
\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq 2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}=2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right).\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq 2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}},\\
\left|\bar{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|\leq 2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\sum_{n_{0}=N_{0}}^{N-1}\sum_{n=1}^{N_{0}}\binom{n_{0}}{n}=2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right).\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Noting that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|=2^{K\sum_{n=1}^{N}=2^{n}}=2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|{\mathcal{F}}_{N}\right|=2^{K\sum_{n=1}^{N}=2^{n}}=2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p">we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex80X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1\geq\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1\geq\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)}-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right)-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)}-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)}-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right)-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K\left(2^{N+1}-1\right)}-2^{K\left(2^{N}-1\right)}\times\left(2^{N}-1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex80Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)-S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)-S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex80Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\frac{S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msup><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\frac{S^{N^{2}}}{2^{K2^{N}}-\left(2^{N}-1\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.5" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\setminus{\mathcal{F}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}{\left|\tilde{{\mathcal{F}}}_{N_{0},N}\right|}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A4.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">D-D</span> </span><span id="A4.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="4. ‣ VI-A Scale Hint Technique ‣ VI Extensions ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a circuit representation <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=\{C_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=\{C_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of non-increasing SRC and denote the corresponding mapping by <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SRC}(f,N_{0})=\operatorname{SRC}(f,N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>SRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>SRC</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SRC}(f,N_{0})=\operatorname{SRC}(f,N)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the definition of SRC, there exists a set of operators <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}=\{g_{1},\dots,g_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}=\{g_{1},\dots,g_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}:\Sigma^{n_{k}}\mapsto\Sigma,n_{k}\leq N_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}:\Sigma^{n_{k}}\mapsto\Sigma,n_{k}\leq N_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define the PRF-SH</p>
<table id="A4.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j,n):=\begin{cases}\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}n_{k}+I^{-1}_{i}(j),&amp;\text{ if }\left(i,g_{k^{\prime}},I_{i}\right)\in C_{n},\\
\sum_{k=1}^{K}n_{k},&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j,n):=\begin{cases}\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}n_{k}+I^{-1}_{i}(j),&amp;\text{ if }\left(i,g_{k^{\prime}},I_{i}\right)\in C_{n},\\
\sum_{k=1}^{K}n_{k},&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We will show that the PRF-SH <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j,n)</annotation></semantics></math> characterizes <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The consistency follows directly from the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. It remains to check the distinctness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For any distinct pairs <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j,m)\neq(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j,m)\neq(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n)</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose that <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,g^{(i)},I_{i})\in C_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,g^{(i)},I_{i})\in C_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in I_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in I_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},g^{(i^{\prime})},I_{i^{\prime}})\in C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},g^{(i^{\prime})},I_{i^{\prime}})\in C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}\in I_{i^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}\in I_{i^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<ul id="A4.I1.i1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(i)}\neq g^{(i^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(i)}\neq g^{(i^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math> (without loss of generality, we assume <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(i)}=g_{k_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(i)}=g_{k_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(i^{\prime})}=g_{k_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(i^{\prime})}=g_{k_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}&lt;k_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}&lt;k_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), then</p>
<table id="A4.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j,m)=\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}-1}n_{k}+I^{-1}_{i}(j)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}}n_{k}&lt;\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}}n_{k}+1\leq\sum_{k=1}^{k_{2}-1}n_{k}+I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n);" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munderover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j,m)=\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}-1}n_{k}+I^{-1}_{i}(j)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}}n_{k}&lt;\sum_{k=1}^{k_{1}}n_{k}+1\leq\sum_{k=1}^{k_{2}-1}n_{k}+I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n);</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(i)}=g^{(i^{\prime})}=g_{k^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(i)}=g^{(i^{\prime})}=g_{k^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A4.I1.i1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{i}^{-1}(j)\neq I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{i}^{-1}(j)\neq I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A4.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi(i,j,m)=\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}+I_{i}^{-1}(j)\neq\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}+I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≠</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j,m)=\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}+I_{i}^{-1}(j)\neq\sum_{k=1}^{k^{\prime}-1}+I_{i^{\prime}}^{-1}(j^{\prime})=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\prime}\not\in I_{i^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\prime}\not\in I_{i^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(i,j,m)&lt;+\infty=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(i,j,m)&lt;+\infty=\phi(i^{\prime},j^{\prime},n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the PRF-SH <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the distinctness condition.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data.</span> When the scale hint is not applied, we align all the instances (except for Select) to the maximum scale by filling with “0”. This is to guarantee the existence of characterizing PRFs for the task. For example, for the copy task where the training instances are of scales 1–5 and the testing instances are of scales 6–10, we align all instances to scale 10. An aligned training instance is like</p>
<table id="A5.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{x_{1}\;x_{2}\;x_{3}\;x_{4}\;x_{5}\;0\;0\;0\;0\;0\;=\;x_{1}\;x_{2}\;x_{3}\;x_{4}\;x_{5}\;0\;0\;0\;0\;0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟹</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟺</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟻</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace"> 0 0 0 0 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟸</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟹</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟺</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟻</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathvariant="monospace"> 0 0 0 0 0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{x_{1}\;x_{2}\;x_{3}\;x_{4}\;x_{5}\;0\;0\;0\;0\;0\;=\;x_{1}\;x_{2}\;x_{3}\;x_{4}\;x_{5}\;0\;0\;0\;0\;0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When the scale hint is applied, we do not align the instances because we can always find a characterizing PRF-SH according to Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="4. ‣ VI-A Scale Hint Technique ‣ VI Extensions ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. An unaligned copy instance of scale <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is like</p>
<table id="A5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mi>𝚗</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mn>𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚡</mi><mi>𝚗</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We summarize the data formats of the tasks in our experiments in Table <a href="#A5.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ Appendix E Experimental Details ‣ On the Limitations and Capabilities of Position Embeddings for Length Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Data formats of the tasks in our experiments.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A5.T1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Task</span></th>
<th id="A5.T1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Unaligned format</span></th>
<th id="A5.T1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Aligned format</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A5.T1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Copy</span></th>
<td id="A5.T1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚗</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚗</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;0\;\dots\;0\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;0\;\dots\;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="monospace"> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="monospace"> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">𝟷</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚡</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝚗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="monospace"> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="monospace"> 0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;0\;\dots\;0\;=\;x_{1}\;\dots\;x_{n}\;0\;\dots\;0}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
